.nh
.TH "true-knowledge" "1" "Sep 2026" "true-knowledge" "tk (true-knowledge)"

.SH NAME
tk-setup - Make this machine ready: init + install backends (+ optional register/client)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtk setup [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Idempotent fresh-machine setup. Re-running changes nothing when up-to-date.
Steps: init dirs/config → install all backends at pins → (opt-in) register cwd → (opt-in) client snippet.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--client\fP=""
	print MCP snippet for pi|opencode|claude|codex

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print plan without downloading or writing

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for setup

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	project name for --register (default: directory base)

.PP
\fB--register\fP[=false]
	register the current directory as a project (opt-in)

.PP
\fB--tool-profile\fP=""
	tool surface for --client (scout|analysis|minimal|memory); emitted as TK_MCP_PROFILE env so per-project overrides work


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--budget\fP=0
	char budget override (0 = config defaults)

.PP
\fB--home\fP=""
	override base home (TK_HOME equivalent: config+data+cache+state under it)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	stable JSON envelope output


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  tk setup
  tk setup --dry-run
  tk setup --register --name demo
  tk setup --client opencode
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtk(1)\fP
